uded one by vince mcmahon and the  federation  that macho man never got over the wwf  planned an old-timers battle royal for a  house show at the meadowlands  in new jersey for november of 1987.  randy savage was at the peak of his  power in the company  he just formed the mega powers with hulk  hogan that october  and had an all-time classic match with  ricky steamboat at wrestlemania 3  earlier in the year as such savage  flexed his political muscles to get his  father into the match  the day of the match came and plenty of  legends were part of it but  no angelo poppo lanny poppo told  bleacher report  randy really loved vince until the  battle royal he felt really bad when al  costello who was one of dad's best  friends in wrestling  said where's your father he should be  here randy never forgot about the battle  royal  he felt guilty like he should have done  more the battle royal snub  was the beginning of the end of savage's  relationship with vince mcmahon by 1994  savage was spending more time as an  announcer than a wrestler he was just  past  40 years old but still felt he could  compete lanny poppo recalled the  bleacher report that his brother  felt he never had a match as good as the  steamboat match but thought he could  recapture that magic with sean michaels  randy wanted to do a two-year program  building up to a match with sean at  wrestlemania randy would lose  retire and go back to the announcer's  table this proposal was shot down  since the federation was in the middle  of a youth movement savage decided to  take his talents elsewhere when his  contract expired which in that  era meant the competing world  championship wrestling  even so breaking off his decade-plus  relationship with vince was daunting  bruce prichard who was vince's right  hand man in that era revealed on his  podcast something to wrestle that randy  had to get drunk  to call vince and tell him he was  quitting only for an irritated benz to  call him back the next day  the t